WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Why can't you pour a brick?

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.850
In a solid, particles are packed tight and only jiggle in place.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:15.770
In a liquid, they still touch, but slide past each other. So it pours.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:21.013
In a gas, they fly apart and fill the whole space they are in.
